  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Road Rapid Tanzania (OSO Enschede): Demonstrating the local use of Water Repellent Paved Roads in Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bad road conditions in Tanzania lead to a variety of issues, such as agricultural products and farmers not reaching the markets in the cities in time, which often results in unnecessary loss of income, food waste and imports from abroad. Road Rapid is an innovative and environment-friendly product using Dutch technology that makes it easy to strengthen unpaved roads, to create water repellent roads and makes these more suitable for heavier transport, especially during the rainy season. With the support of Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) the company OSO Enschede constructed a test road of one kilometre to demonstrate the feasibility and local adaptability of Road Rapid in the Tanzanian context. Road Rapid can be applied using existing machinery and equipment of local road constructors and showed to be considerably cheaper than asphalted roads, which in turn has the potential to create competitive advantage for local companies using the product, improve existing production processes and lead to better infrastructure. The project successfully demonstrated its feasibility and provided the business case for further expansion of Road Rapid in Tanzania. The project directly supported 27 jobs, indirectly supported 20 jobs and trained 10 people on how to use Road Rapid in existing construction methods.</narrative>
  </description>
